Subject: [PATCH] docs(sensitivity): state the exact linear OVB identity behind
 gamma x delta

Clarify that the sensitivity shift is an exact linear omitted-variable-bias
identity when gamma is the auxiliary-regression coefficient, that unit-variance
U alone is not sufficient, how the bias scales with the intervention contrast,
and that the fixed shift does not propagate uncertainty. Correct the
calibration benchmark. Docstrings and prose only; no behaviour change.

Fixes #157
